**Authors:** Mike A. Lund, Akshaykumar Salimath, Kjetil M. D. Hals
**Affiliation:** Dept. of Engineering Sciences, University of Agder, Norway
**arXiv:** 2106.15187v2 [cond-mat.mes-hall]

## Abstract
The ac spin pumping of noncollinear antiferromagnets is theoretically
investigated. Starting from an effective action description, the Onsager
coefficients connecting spin pumping and spin-transfer torque of the
SO(3)-valued order parameter are derived, then applied to a kagome
antiferromagnet resonantly driven by a uniform field. The three spin-wave
bands of the kagome AF generate spin currents with mutually orthogonal
polarization directions.

## Section III — kagome Hamiltonian
$$H = J\sum_{\langle ij\rangle} \mathbf S_i\cdot\mathbf S_j
   + \sum_i\left[ K_z (\mathbf S_i\cdot\hat e_z)^2 - K(\mathbf S_i\cdot\hat n_i)^2\right]$$

Resonance frequencies of the three k=0 spin-wave bands:
$$\omega_0^{(x)}=\omega_0^{(y)}=\sqrt{4K_1 a_2/a_1^2},\qquad
  \omega_0^{(z)}=\sqrt{4K_2 a_2/a_1^2}.$$

